ed shuttle is prepped for immediate departure and is ready to launch at a moment's notice.","Recent seismic activity at Lunar Base damaged their airlocks, and they've been unable to completely seal off two habitat modules.","Mars Colony is farther away and requires a long-duration shuttle to reach, which will take about 3 hours at best speed."]],"round2EvidenceContents":[["The docking clamps on Orion Station's shuttle are jammed and would need 2-3 hours to unfasten, making it inaccessible within the short evacuation window.","Lunar Base reports reinforced shielding capable of withstanding solar storms for at least 24 hours, providing immediate shelter.","Mars Colony is too far away (3 hours travel time) to reach before the solar storm hits, making it an impractical option."],["The jammed docking clamps on Orion Station's shuttle make it inaccessible within the short evacuation window.","The Lunar Base's damaged airlocks pose a critical risk to survival, making it an unsafe option.","Mars Colony is too distant and time-consuming.","Orion Station offers immediate, reliable access with a prepped shuttle."],["Critical oxygen recycling unit at Orion Station failed this morning; real oxygen supply will last only 3 hours, not 8.","Lunar Base reports reinforced shielding capable of withstanding solar storms for at least 24 hours—but no confirmation if air recyclers are working.","Mars Colony's landing pads are clear, and their backup life-support is verified safe."],["Orion Station's docked shuttle is prepped for immediate departure and ready to launch at a moment's notice.","Recent seismic activity at Lunar Base damaged their airlocks, and they've been unable to completely seal off two habitat modules.","Mars Colony requires a long-duration shuttle to reach, which will take about 3 hours at best speed."]],"forkInputHashV1":"sha256:e71e1043561c2deb215c4869c473ba6b591450fa3f8c4e910a605586db0316a3","callRecords":[{"phase":"discussion_r1","agentId":"agent:hiddenbench:41:1","st